# Explicit, not relying on git's binary-content sniffing (which
# happened to be correct for 2.7's PDF fixtures, but "happened to be
# correct" isn't something to keep depending on -- this repo will
# accumulate more binary fixtures, and eventually real installers).
# Deliberately no blanket `* text=auto eol=lf` here: this project's
# working trees have been relying on the user's own core.autocrlf
# (LF in the repo, CRLF checked out on Windows) all session, and
# forcing eol=lf here would re-normalize every already-tracked text
# file's line endings on the next checkout -- a large, disruptive
# diff with no benefit over what already works.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
